 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Who",
     "texto": [
      "With verbs such as **ждать** (to wait for), **знать** (to know), **приглашать** (to invite) and **встречать** (to meet or receive), the person goes in the accusative. To ask «who?» you say **Кого?**: **Кого ты ждёшь?** (who are you waiting for?).",
      "Examples: **Я жду брата** (I'm waiting for my brother), **Я знаю Анну** (I know Anna), **Я приглашаю сестру** (I invite my sister) and **Я встречаю друга** (I'm meeting a friend)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Personal pronouns",
     "texto": [
      "Pronouns change too: **тебя** (you), **его** (him), **её** (her), **их** (them). You say **Я люблю тебя** (I love you).",
      "**Любить** and **ждать** follow the same pattern: what you feel or wait for goes in the accusative."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
